---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="How to Choose the Perfect Mid-Drive Motor for a Folding eBike | Geektion Insights">
	<main class="container mx-auto p-4 py-20 max-w-4xl">
		<header class="mb-16 text-center">
			<h3 class="text-cyberBlue font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">B2B Buying Guide</h3>
			<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-8 leading-tight tracking-tighter uppercase text-white">How to Choose the Perfect Mid-Drive Motor for a Folding eBike</h1>
			<p class="text-xl opacity-60 font-light italic leading-relaxed">A practical selection framework for brand owners, engineers, and wholesalers entering the folding eBike segment.</p>
		</header>

		<div class="aspect-video mb-12 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden bg-black relative group">
			<img 
				src="https://sc02.alicdn.com/kf/H1ed28ff0c43f4948ac6d4621addc1ce4v.jpg" 
				alt="Mid-drive motor integrated into a folding eBike frame" 
				class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-80 group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-700"
			/>
		</div>

		<article class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8 opacity-80 leading-relaxed text-lg text-silver">
			<p>
				The folding eBike market is booming—and with it, the demand for drive systems that disappear into the frame instead of dominating it. But choosing the right mid-drive motor for a folding platform is not a simple spec-sheet comparison. The constraints of a folding frame change every engineering rule.
			</p>
			<p>
				At Geektion, we engineer specifically for these constraints. Our Micro Mid-Drive systems are the result of hundreds of integration tests on 16" and 20" folding platforms. Here is the selection framework we share with B2B partners before they commit to a platform.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-tighter pt-8 border-l-4 border-cyberBlue pl-6">The 4-Point Selection Checklist</h2>

			<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-cyberBlue uppercase tracking-tight">1. Weight: The Forgotten Spec</h3>
			<p>
				For a folding bike, weight isn't about performance—it's about <em>portability</em>. A drive system exceeding 3kg instantly destroys the "pick-up-and-carry" advantage of the platform. Aim for a complete system under 2.5kg. The Geektion C-Series achieves 2.1kg with the motor, controller, and wiring harness fully integrated.
			</p>

			<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-cyberBlue uppercase tracking-tight">2. Torque: Match It To The Wheel Size</h3>
			<p>
				Small wheels (16"-20") multiply effective torque. A 60Nm motor on a 20" wheel feels significantly stronger than the same motor on a 26" wheel. This is why our C-Series is tuned to 45-60Nm—enough for steep city grades without wasting battery on unnecessary peak power.
			</p>

			<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-cyberBlue uppercase tracking-tight">3. Integration: The Folding Geometry Test</h3>
			<p>
				The motor must not interfere with the fold. Verify the bottom bracket dimensions (standard 68mm), cable routing options, and whether the motor housing creates clearance issues at the hinge point. Our <a href="/solutions/drive-system" class="text-cyberBlue underline hover:text-white transition-colors">E-Drive Series</a> was designed with a 110mm-diameter stealth housing specifically to pass this test.
			</p>

			<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-cyberBlue uppercase tracking-tight">4. Certification: Selling Across Borders</h3>
			<p>
				If you distribute globally, motor compliance is a market-access issue. Verify EN15194 (EU), UL2849 (US), and IP rating (we recommend IP67 for reliability). A system that fails certification locks you out of key markets.
			</p>

			<div class="my-12 border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-8">
				<h4 class="text-white font-bold tracking-tighter mb-6 uppercase">Quick Comparison Checklist</h4>
				<div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm font-mono">
					<div class="flex justify-between border-b border-white/10 pb-2"><span class="opacity-60">System Weight</span><span class="text-cyberBlue">&lt; 2.5 kg</span></div>
					<div class="flex justify-between border-b border-white/10 pb-2"><span class="opacity-60">Nominal Torque</span><span class="text-cyberBlue">45 - 60 Nm</span></div>
					<div class="flex justify-between border-b border-white/10 pb-2"><span class="opacity-60">BB Compatibility</span><span class="text-cyberBlue">68mm Standard</span></div>
					<div class="flex justify-between border-b border-white/10 pb-2"><span class="opacity-60">Compliance</span><span class="text-cyberBlue">EN15194 / UL2849</span></div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-tighter pt-8">Why Architecture Matters: Read the In-runner Deep-Dive</h2>
			<p>
				Beyond the checklist, the internal motor architecture determines real-world feel and longevity. To understand why our high-RPM in-runner design delivers the instantaneous torque response folding bikes need, read our full technical comparison: <a href="/insights/in-runner-vs-out-runner" class="text-cyberBlue underline hover:text-white transition-colors">In-runner vs. Out-runner Motors</a>.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-tighter pt-8">Conclusion: Start With The Right Foundation</h2>
			<p>
				The folding eBike segment rewards brands that get the fundamentals right. Weight, torque calibration, fold-safe integration, and certification—get these four right, and you have a product that sells itself. Get them wrong, and no amount of marketing will fix it.
			</p>
			<p>
				Our engineering team provides integration drawings and prototype support to qualifying partners. <a href="/contact" class="text-cyberBlue underline hover:text-white transition-colors">Contact our B2B team</a> to start your evaluation.
			</p>
		</article>

		<div class="mt-20 pt-12 border-t border-white/10 text-center">
			<h4 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest opacity-50 mb-8 font-bold text-cyberBlue">Explore the Full Drive System Series</h4>
			<div class="flex justify-center">
				<a href="/solutions/drive-system" class="px-8 py-4 bg-industrialOrange text-white font-bold uppercase tracking-widest hover:bg-white hover:text-industrialOrange transition-all tracking-tighter">
					View E-Drive Technical Specs
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>
